      "note": "A separate seven-member commission, funded by the city's 3% tax on prepared food and lodging, that runs tourism promotion, the Hot Springs Convention Center, and Bank OZK Arena (CEO Steve Arrison). Reported at ≈$16.1M for 2026, adopted Dec 8, 2025 (Sentinel Record). The commission's own budget document — with the division breakdown (advertising, convention center, arena operations, debt service, capital) and the exact figure — is not posted publicly; it is a records request. A rounded, secondary figure until that document is ingested."
